WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.600
Russia freed 74-year-old Stephen Hubbard as Whitcoff brought Putin a Ukraine piece proposal. This is Omni View Top World News, episode 29. I'm Mira. The Nerra Network's AI host. Kenya is dealing with a first Ebola outbreak. Gulf oil is moving above pre-war volumes, and Britain has cleared a North Sea gas field, with a sign of progress at the end. In St. Petersburg, President Vladimir Putin sat down with U.S. envoy Steve Whitcoff for a ninth face-to-face meeting on the war.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:33.540
The Globe and Mail says the session opened inside the Constantine Palace, with investment

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.480
envoy Karel Demetriyev in the room.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.840
Hubbard is a retired teacher from Michigan.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.180
Prosecutor said he served in a defense unit in Iseum.

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.080
He denies that mercenary charge.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:46.580
A closed trial in 2024 gave him nearly seven years.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:51.220
The State Department had called him wrongfully detained, and Russian State media said he

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:52.800
was taken to Polkhov airport.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:57.800
After the meeting, Whitkov called Tuesday's Oslo talks with President Volodymyr Zelensky

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:02.100
constructive, and said a cease-fire can be built on a foundation that already exists.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:06.200
He wants Putin to consider three-way talks with Kiev on the technical points.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:11.340
Secretary of State Marco Rubio called the Oslo session positive, and said those ideas

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:12.700
would go to the Russian side.

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:17.980
Zelensky said Oslo also settled disruptions to intelligent sharing and to the Star-Shield

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:18.760
satellite link.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:23.800
President Donald Trump said Ukraine must end the war or face a very bad thing, and that

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:26.360
Zelensky's own people will not stand for holding out.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:30.040
Putin still wants all of Denetsk and no NATO place for Ukraine.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:35.380
He told Whitcoff that Moscow can help on the Iran crisis, and wants economic ties restored.

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:39.960
He said the first cargo under this month's diesel deal with Washington leaves in two to

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:40.440
three days.

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:45.080
Foreign Minister Sergei Lavrov said Moscow will listen and expect no miracle.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:50.860
Norway's Prime Minister, Jonas Garstor, said Whitcoff plans to come back to Oslo, and

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:53.100
that Russia may be looking for a diplomatic opening.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:57.100
Russia also says its line on an energy ceasefire has not changed.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:59.180
It wants a peace, not a truce.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:03.920
On the satellite fight, the Wall Street Journal reported that Elon Musk ordered a star-shield

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:04.560
slowdown.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:06.420
Reuters could not verify that.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:08.580
Trump says he did not order restrictions.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:12.220
Rubio says Washington has not cut Kiev's Starlink access.

00:02:13.397 --> 00:02:15.257
Kenya isn't its first Ebola outbreak.

00:02:15.737 --> 00:02:18.177
The BBC says nine people have tested positive.

00:02:18.557 --> 00:02:22.857
Every one of them tied to a man who came from the Democratic Republic of Congo and died

00:02:22.857 --> 00:02:28.077
two weeks ago. Four relatives, three health workers, and a hospital cleaner make up the rest.

00:02:28.497 --> 00:02:33.497
The United States has told its citizens to think again before traveling there. Uganda, Ethiopia,

00:02:33.837 --> 00:02:39.197
and Somalia are watching their borders. The virus is the Bundy Bugio species. There is no approved

00:02:39.197 --> 00:02:44.357
vaccine and no approved treatment, though trials are running. The International Rescue Committee counts

00:02:44.357 --> 00:02:50.917
more than 9,500 cases in Congo since May, and more than 4,000 deaths. The second deadliest outbreak

00:02:50.917 --> 00:02:56.377
on record. That traffic is why a regional hub stays exposed. Health Director General Patrick

00:02:56.377 --> 00:03:00.957
Amath said Tuesday night that the eight living patients are improving. Kenya is screening

00:03:00.957 --> 00:03:06.177
arrivals from 10 countries it calls high risk, with a digital form and a QR code, and it has

00:03:06.177 --> 00:03:12.797
set aside isolation beds plus a separate test lab at Kenyatta National Hospital. 134 of 135

00:03:12.797 --> 00:03:17.877
listed contacts are in quarantine. The Rescue Committee reads that is assigned the first response

00:03:17.877 --> 00:03:21.237
is holding. Doctors' Union representative Dennis Muskella

00:03:21.237 --> 00:03:25.697
told the BBC the borders, the ports, and the main airport are badly short of staff.

00:03:26.826 --> 00:03:30.066
Oil leaving the Middle East, through the Strait of Hormuz and around it,

00:03:30.266 --> 00:03:33.306
is above the pre-war pace even while ships are still being hit.

00:03:33.926 --> 00:03:37.246
Iran wire carried a Wall Street Journal reading of Kepler's trackers.

00:03:37.606 --> 00:03:42.586
In the week ending the 18th of October, regional exports top 24 million barrels a day.

00:03:42.986 --> 00:03:47.726
Before the war, the figure was 23.3 million. Hormuz itself is caring about

00:03:47.726 --> 00:03:51.326
14 million barrels a day, 82 percent of the old volume.

00:03:51.706 --> 00:03:56.106
The journal treats that shortfall as evidence Iran is less able to choke the region's oil,

00:03:56.606 --> 00:04:01.766
pointing to U.S. naval escorts, transfers off Oman, and pipelines in Saudi Arabia and

00:04:01.766 --> 00:04:02.986
the United Arab Emirates.

00:04:03.386 --> 00:04:07.506
In September, about 40 percent of crude from Gulf states other than Iran's skipped

00:04:07.506 --> 00:04:10.666
hormones, before the war that share was 17 percent.

00:04:11.206 --> 00:04:15.746
Maritime reports cited by the paper logged about 30 attacks on vessels in October alone.

00:04:15.746 --> 00:04:22.146
Moving one barrel from the Gulf to China on a very large carrier now costs roughly $37.37.

00:04:22.706 --> 00:04:27.166
War risk cover has climbed to as much as 10 percent of a ship's value in some cases.

00:04:27.786 --> 00:04:30.146
Owners are still sailing because the margins are high.

00:04:30.686 --> 00:04:35.426
Iran's own exports, the same account says, have nearly stopped under a U.S. blockade

00:04:35.426 --> 00:04:35.786
